    "completionTimestamp": "JSON event ts minus lastCompletionAgeMs; approximate due timestamp generation after capture snapshot.",
    "threadCpuSemantics": "thread_time_ns bracket immediately around resource.grab; nonCPU = monotonic wall bracket minus that capture thread CPU. Includes waiting, descheduling and native/system work outside measured thread CPU; does not name the cause.",
    "processCpuSemantics": "Difference of RUSAGE_SELF user+system cumulative CPU between adjacent event rows divided by wall interval *100; 100% means one logical CPU, whole Host process, coarse 5-6 second window.",
    "eventLoopSemantics": "eventLoop max/p95 summarize rolling 60 second sampled window; not exact temporal alignment to last grab. systemLoad1 is host load average, not CPU utilization.",
    "populationLimitation": "Only last completed grab at each ~5-6 second telemetry sample, plus track lifetime maxima. Cannot derive full-frame latency distribution, total slow-frame count, or CPU saturation of machine from these rows."
